      "math_academy_id": "q-108635",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the First Term of an Arithmetic Series Given the Common Difference and the Sum",
      "problem": "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=0.6,$ and the sum of the first $37$ terms is ${S}_{37}=444?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=37$, $d=0.6$, and ${S}_{N}=444$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}444 & =\\frac{37}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(37-1)(0.6)) \\\\ 888 & =37(2{a}_{1}+21.6) \\\\ \\frac{888}{37} & =2{a}_{1}+21.6 \\\\ 2.4 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
